 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "This Thursday, you left again\nThe light of your face and forehead;\nAnd now these shadows darken again.\nIt is enough for me to remember\nThat I have seen the world without me,\nOr parted, as a lovely,\nIn any good day or evil hour.\nThere was no one here before again.\nAh! little thing this one beauty remains,\nThe veil which covers it so; but again\nWe will pass away together again.\nMarch 1945. (A requiem poem",
